==================== Instruction ====================
I want to create a webpage that implements a purely front-end-based job competency modeling and simulation system. HR professionals can search for competency models by job name or keywords, and the page will display a list of results and access detailed information. On the details page, the system needs to represent the competency model as a directed weighted graph structure, with nodes representing competencies and edges representing dependencies or reinforcement relationships. Users can directly drag and drop to adjust competency levels, modify weights, or temporarily enable/disable certain competencies. The page needs to recalculate competency coverage, critical paths, and risk competency gaps in real time after each structural change, and immediately alert users to potential problems. The system should provide a general job competency model template library, allowing HR professionals to quickly build models and save custom templates. It should also support scenario-based simulations for recruitment, training, and promotion, simulating the impact of model adjustments under different scenarios.
