trating a measurable impact on key indicators after running the simulation.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Explicit \\\"Save\\\" does not actually persist edited model state\", \"actual\": \"After running a Promotion simulation (which changed Critical Path from 3 to 4 competencies) and clicking the header \\\"Save\\\" button (which showed a \\\"Model Saved - Your changes have been saved successfully\\\" toast), navigating away to the home page and back into the Software Engineer model reverted Critical Path back to the original 3 competencies (Programming Languages, Problem Solving, System Design) and Weight Change/Level Change sliders reset to 0. The save action gives a false success confirmation but does not actually persist state.\", \"evidence\": \"Pre-save/post-simulation: Critical Path=4 competencies. Post \\\"Model Saved\\\" toast, navigate away and back: Critical Path=3 competencies (reverted), scenario adjustments reset to 0.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Cannot verify prevention of invalid operations because prerequisite disable functionality is broken\", \"actual\": \"The constraint requires preventing invalid operations such as adding dependency edges to disabled capabilities, but the enable/disable switch on competency nodes does not work at all (confirmed in FT-5: aria-checked never toggles). Since no node can ever actually become disabled, there is no mechanism in the app that could enforce this constraint — the safety net is effectively absent. Additionally, attempting to draw a new edge between nodes via connection handles (dragging from a source handle to a target handle) did not create any new edge (edge count remained 5), suggesting the app may not support user-initiated edge creation via the graph UI at all, further preventing verification of edge-related validation rules.\", \"evidence\": \"Edge count before and after a handle-to-handle drag attempt remained 5; node switch aria-checked never changes per FT-5 findings.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Adjusting the \\\"Weight Change\\\" slider for the technical category (via keyboard ArrowRight, +5%) in the Recruitment scenario tab immediately updated the Coverage indicator from 68% to 72% and Avg Level from 3.3 to 3.5, without needing to click \\\"Run Simulation\\\" — demonstrating real-time recalculation of the coverage percentage in response to model adjustments.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph canvas (6 nodes, 5 edges — moderate complexity) responds smoothly to zoom controls (scale changed from 0.736 to 0.883 immediately on \\\"zoom in\\\" click) and to node drag-and-drop (confirmed in FT-3, position updates immediately via CSS transform with no lag/hang). Pan/minimap/fit-view controls are present and functional, indicating responsive graph editing interactions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph renders 6 competency nodes and 5 edges using React Flow. Each edge has marker-end=\\\"url('#...type=arrowclosed')\\\" confirming directed arrows, and each edge displays a percentage weight label (e.g. \\\"80%\\\", \\\"70%\\\", \\\"90%\\\", \\\"60%\\\", \\\"50%\\\") plus accessible names like \\\"Edge from prog-lang to code-review\\\" — clearly conveying a directed, weighted graph structure of competencies (nodes) and dependencies (edges).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Critical Path indicator recalculates after structural changes: running a Promotion scenario simulation (weight adjustments) changed Critical Path from 3 competencies (Programming Languages, Problem Solving, System Design) to 4 competencies (Problem Solving, Programming Languages, Collaboration, +1), displayed prominently in the top stats bar with named competencies listed — confirming real-time recalculation and prominent highlighting of the critical path after a model-affecting change.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Risk Gaps indicator never updates and underlying calculation is unstable\", \"actual\": \"The \\\"Risk Gaps\\\" stat consistently showed \\\"0 identified\\\" across all tested structural/scenario changes, including running Recruitment simulation with +5% technical weight change and Promotion simulation with -5% technical/+10% behavioral weight changes — no risk gap was ever surfaced even though such adjustments substantially changed Coverage and Critical Path. Additionally, repeatedly pressing ArrowLeft on the \\\"Level Change\\\" slider (attempting a negative adjustment) corrupted the slider's value to aria-valuenow=\\\"NaN\\\", and after running a simulation, the Coverage and Avg Level stats also displayed \\\"NaN%\\\"/\\\"NaN\\\"/\\\"N/A\\\", indicating the underlying calculation engine is unstable and the Risk Gaps warning analysis does not reliably function.\", \"evidence\": \"Risk Gaps remained \\\"0 identified\\\" through all simulation runs; Coverage displayed \\\"NaN%\\\" and Avg Level \\\"NaN\\\"/\\\"N/A\\\" after a second simulation run; Level Change slider aria-valuenow became \\\"NaN\\\" after multiple ArrowLeft key presses.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No functional prompt/warning UI ever surfaces for detected problems\", \"actual\": \"The only candidate UI for problem prompts is the \\\"Risk Gaps\\\" stat card (with a warning-style icon) in the top summary bar, but it remained \\\"0 identified\\\" throughout all tests regardless of significant model changes (simulations, weight/level adjustments), so no actual text/icon warning was ever observed to appear. The \\\"Analytics\\\" nav link (which might otherwise host a dedicated warnings/insights view) is a non-functional placeholder (href=\\\"#\\\") that do